        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br>Set $x = -1$: $3(-1) + 5 = A(1) + B(0)$ \u2192 $2 = A$.<br>Set $x = -2$: $3(-2) + 5 = A(0) + B(-1)$ \u2192 $-1 = -B$ \u2192 $B = 1$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{2}{x + 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$.</p>",
